// extended Hewer gain was exact but hewerGainSubstituted rejected it against
// the ddGain of the rounded X, 1.2e-4 from it at a tolerance of 1.7e-9, and
// Dare kept the refined K at Accuracy 1 (DSXP26; rv48Gen 797 natively, X
// 9.7e-11 off the 320-bit X). acc0 are the platforms and NoScaling values on
// which K is exact at Accuracy 0 where the base code held Accuracy 1; the
// literals are those rv48Gen and rv49vGen form there (OSLSY3). Elsewhere a
// row need only not be certified-wrong, and is not discriminating: rv48 797
// and rv49 107 on amd64, rv49 4325 natively, where 107 and 4325 stay Accuracy
// 1 with K beyond its band as on the base code. Under gonum 30740af (HF5PTS)
// rv48 797 NoScaling false and rv49 107 natively, and rv49 4325 on amd64,
